                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "i had fun...until this game became real frustrating. So much so that i got a headache. read some of the other negative reviews. They are applicable.\nFirstly, i like the progression, buy, sell, then profit. Its fun. It was fun...then i found that it was arbitrarily decided that you can't have more than one caboose...basically you have just five characters. Then I find that there is no way to  change that. Then the...frustrations happened. pick up cargo for a contract, already loaded it up, but i find my train is over loaded-then why allow me to load it up? a red text telling me it can't be done. Or i find i can't make it on time to the destination before even rolling, but after i already accepted the contract. But it has a fucking penalty fee? WHO THE FUCK TAKEs A CONTRACT WITH A PENALTY WITHOUT CHECKING THAT THEY CAN GET THERE ON TIME?! I know that the challenge is for me to do the work of planning....but i was literally bashing my head against the damn desk.\nIf someone offered a contract in real life, the one giving the contract would double check too right? Like: \"all this cargo is too much for your obviously puny train, should you maybe upgrade to increase the power?\"  not \"Here's the cargo, looks like you are overburdened, but hey that's your problem\"\nThere's more too, but I'm done. it's fun, but i keep finding limits, and frustrations that don't make it fun the further I get in the game. \nLike, you are supposed to feel sorry for the natives....but they ask for fucking bribes like bandits? SO i just say fuck you, and just shoot them down. Hell i just shoot everything down just for the xp...or try, since i keep dying and having to restart. Legendary steam machines my ass.",
